  <h2 id="environment">Runtime environment</h2>
  <p>
    <code>environment()</code> returns the effective
    {" "}<code>distribution</code>, <code>applicationOrigin</code>, and
    {" "}<code>credentialStorage</code>. Portable files report origin
    {" "}<code>null</code> and default to <code>memory</code>. A caller-supplied
    storage or key adapter reports <code>custom</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="authorization">MdbaseConnect methods</h2>
  <p>
    Every asynchronous method accepts a final{" "}
    <code>ConnectRequestOptions</code> argument, with <code>signal</code> and
    {" "}<code>timeoutMs</code>, and resolves to a <code>ConnectOutcome</code>.
  </p>
  <table class="api-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Method</th>
        <th>Result</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>application(options)</code></td><td><code>MdbaseApplicationSession</code></td><td>The ordinary application lifecycle entry point</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>register(options?)</code></td><td><code>ConnectOutcome&lt;Application&gt;</code></td><td>Load, canonicalize, and register the bundled manifest</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>manifest(options?)</code></td><td><code>ConnectOutcome&lt;MdbaseApplicationManifest&gt;</code></td><td>The loaded, validated manifest</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>authorize(options?)</code></td><td><code>ConnectOutcome&lt;MdbaseAuthorizationOutcome&gt;</code></td><td>Registry-level authorization; applications normally use the session</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>completeAuthorization(callbackUrl?, options?)</code></td><td><code>ConnectOutcome&lt;MdbaseAuthorizationResult&gt;</code></td><td>Complete a web or native callback</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>connections()</code></td><td><code>MdbaseConnectionInfo[]</code></td><td>Every saved collection authorization for this application</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>connection(collectionId)</code></td><td><code>MdbaseConnection | null</code></td><td>One permanently collection-bound client</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>unavailableReason(collectionId)</code></td><td><code>MdbaseUnavailableReason | null</code></td><td>Why a saved collection cannot be used</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>onConnectionsChange(listener)</code></td><td>Unsubscribe function</td><td>Observe additions, removal, refresh, and cross-tab storage changes</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>environment()</code></td><td><code>MdbaseConnectEnvironment</code></td><td>Distribution, origin, and credential storage in effect</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>forgetAll()</code></td><td><code>void</code></td><td>Forget every locally retained connection for this application</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <h3>Portable authorization options</h3>
  <p>
    <code>authorize()</code> on the manager or session accepts
    {" "}<code>onDeviceCode</code> to report
    {" "}<code>userCode</code>, <code>verificationUri</code>,
    {" "}<code>verificationUriComplete</code>, <code>expiresAt</code>, and
    {" "}<code>intervalSeconds</code>. Supply <code>openVerification</code> to own
    the approval window, or an <code>AbortSignal</code> to cancel polling and
    discard the unapproved key.
  </p>

  <h2 id="session">MdbaseApplicationSession</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={session} language="ts" label="Browser application boundary" />
  <p>
    One session owns collection selection, authorization, setup checks, and a
    snapshot. <code>MdbaseBrowserSelection</code> keeps the selected
    collection in the URL and follows back and forward navigation; native
    shells supply their own selection adapter.
  </p>
  <table class="api-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Method</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>start(options?)</code></td><td>Load the manifest and restore the selected collection; concurrent callers share the work</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>subscribe(listener)</code>, <code>getSnapshot()</code></td><td>External-store state: <code>unselected</code>, <code>authorization_required</code>, <code>checking_setup</code>, <code>setup_review_required</code>, <code>ready</code>, <code>unavailable</code>, <code>blocked</code>, and start-up states</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>connection()</code></td><td>The ready collection's <code>MdbaseConnection</code>, or <code>null</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>authorize(target, options?)</code></td><td>Authorize <code>"choose"</code>, <code>"selected"</code>, or <code>{`{ collectionId }`}</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>completeAuthorization(callbackUrl?, options?)</code></td><td>Complete the callback; the snapshot becomes <code>ready</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>ensureCapabilities(capabilities, options?)</code></td><td>Request declared optional capabilities; <code>unchanged</code> when already granted</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>applyCollectionSetup(options?)</code></td><td>Apply reviewed collection setup</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>select(collectionId)</code>, <code>clearSelection()</code>, <code>forget(collectionId)</code></td><td>Change or forget the selection</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>destroy()</code></td><td>End the session</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Collection IDs are bookmark-safe locators.</strong>
    <p>
      They may appear in history, logs, and shared URLs. They do not authorize
      an operation. Connect still requires the application's stored grant and
      enforces it at the collection authority.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="operations">Collection operations</h2>
  <p>
    The methods below belong to <code>MdbaseConnection</code>, not the manager.
    A repository that holds one connection cannot accidentally read or write a
    different collection when the user changes another part of the UI.
  </p>
  <table class="api-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Method</th>
        <th>Capability</th>
        <th>Notes</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>describe()</code></td><td><code>collection.read</code></td><td>Types, contracts, schemas, settings, and supported operations</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>changes(input?)</code></td><td><code>collection.read</code></td><td>One resumable cursor page</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>watch(options?)</code></td><td><code>collection.read</code></td><td>Bounded start-up, then a subscription with retry, status, and <code>close()</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>read(&#123; path &#125;)</code></td><td><code>collection.read</code></td><td>Effective and raw frontmatter plus revision; <code>file_not_found</code> when missing</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>query(input?)</code></td><td><code>collection.read</code></td><td>One query page</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>queryPages(input?, options?)</code></td><td><code>collection.read</code></td><td>Snapshot-consistent pages, one outcome each</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>queryAll(input?, options?)</code></td><td><code>collection.read</code></td><td>Load every page into one result</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>create(input)</code></td><td><code>records.create</code></td><td>Typed frontmatter and optional body</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>update(input)</code></td><td><code>records.edit</code></td><td>Canonical <code>patch</code>, optional <code>body</code>, and <code>ifRevision</code>; <code>concurrent_modification</code> when stale</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>preflightRename(input)</code></td><td><code>records.edit</code></td><td>Read-only reference impact</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>rename(input)</code></td><td><code>records.edit</code></td><td>Move with optional reference updates</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>renameWithProgress(input, options)</code></td><td><code>records.edit</code></td><td>Preflight reuse, cancellation, and outcome recovery</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>preflightDelete(input)</code></td><td><code>records.delete</code></td><td>Read-only backlink impact</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>delete(input)</code></td><td><code>records.delete</code></td><td>Delete with optional backlink check</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>deleteWithProgress(input, options)</code></td><td><code>records.delete</code></td><td>Preflight reuse, cancellation, and outcome recovery</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>validate(input?)</code></td><td><code>collection.read</code></td><td>Canonical collection validation result</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Saved views and type source</h3>
  <p>
    Saved view methods are <code>listViews()</code>,
    <code>executeView()</code>, <code>readViewSource()</code>,
    <code>createViewSource()</code>, <code>updateViewSource()</code>, and
    {" "}<code>deleteViewSource()</code>. Type source methods are{" "}
    <code>readType()</code>, <code>createType()</code>, and{" "}
    <code>updateType()</code>. Updates require the source revision.
  </p>

  <h2 id="records">Record sessions</h2>
  <p>
    <code>connection.records.open(path, options?)</code> returns a lease on
    the one shared <code>MdbaseRecordSession</code> for that record;
    {" "}<code>connection.records.follow(watch)</code> keeps open sessions
    current. Sessions provide <code>setBody()</code>,
    {" "}<code>patchFrontmatter()</code>, <code>save()</code>,
    {" "}<code>flush()</code>, <code>refresh()</code>, <code>resolve()</code>,
    {" "}<code>discard()</code>, <code>subscribe()</code> and
    {" "}<code>getSnapshot()</code>. See <a href="/sdk/editing/">Editing
    records</a>.
  </p>

